IMPORT `wa-interpretation-act-1984`
IMPORT `cat-act-facts`
IMPORT `cat-regulations-2012`
IMPORT `part-1-preliminary`
IMPORT `part-2-div-2-microchipping`
IMPORT `part-2-div-3-sterilisation`

-- Cat Act 2011 (WA), compilation 00-l0-01, currency start 25 Sep 2025 (mrdoc_48898).
-- Part 2 Division 1 -- Registration and tagging: ss 5-13 (Subdivision 1, ss 5-7; Subdivision 2,
-- ss 8-13). LQA run cat-act-2011-lqa, step 4A, 2026-10-01.
-- Divisions 2 and 3 are imported for ss 9(3)-(4), which refer to ss 14(2) and 18(2).

§ `Section 5 -- Cats to be registered`

-- s 5(2)(a) "the cat has been kept by the person for less than 14 days". "The person" is the
-- owner whose duty is in question.
-- FORK-03, reading A (taken): an owner who is an owner through someone else's keeping -- a
-- parent under s 4(1)(c), an owner of a business that keeps the cat -- has kept the cat from
-- the day that keeping began.
GIVEN n IS A STRING, ks IS A LIST OF `Keeper`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Calendar date`
`the day` n `began keeping the cat, among` ks MEANS
    CONSIDER ks
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
    WHEN k FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        CONSIDER k
        WHEN `an individual` p since THEN
            IF (p's `name`) EQUALS n OR n `is among` (p's `parents or guardians`)
            THEN JUST since
            ELSE `the day` n `began keeping the cat, among` rest
        WHEN `a business or organisation` b owners since THEN
            IF n `is among` (`the names of` owners)
            THEN JUST since
            ELSE `the day` n `began keeping the cat, among` rest

-- FORK-03, reading B: only the person's own keeping counts.
GIVEN n IS A STRING, ks IS A LIST OF `Keeper`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Calendar date`
`reading B -- the day` n `began keeping the cat, among` ks MEANS
    CONSIDER ks
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
    WHEN k FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        CONSIDER k
        WHEN `an individual` p since THEN
            IF (p's `name`) EQUALS n THEN JUST since ELSE `reading B -- the day` n `began keeping the cat, among` rest
        OTHERWISE `reading B -- the day` n `began keeping the cat, among` rest

-- FORK-04, reading A (taken): a duration "for less than 14 days" running from a day is counted
-- as Interpretation Act s 61(1)(b) counts a period reckoned from a day: the first day is not
-- counted, so on day t the cat has been kept for (t - first day) days, and the exemption ends
-- on the 14th day after the first.
-- An owner with no recorded keeping (a registered owner who does not keep the cat, a person
-- taken to keep it under s 4(2)) is treated as not within s 5(2)(a): see ENCODING-NOTES.md.
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 5(2)(a); Interpretation Act 1984 s 61(1)(b) (FORKS 03, 04 reading A)
GIVEN c IS A `Cat`, o IS A `Person`, t IS A `Calendar date`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 5(2)(a) -- the cat` c `has been kept by` o `for less than 14 days on` t IF
    CONSIDER `the day` (o's `name`) `began keeping the cat, among` (c's `keepers`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST since THEN `s 61(1)(g) -- the number of days between` since `and` t LESS THAN 14

-- FORK-04, reading B: both the first day and day t are counted.
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 5(2)(a) (FORK-04 reading B)
GIVEN c IS A `Cat`, o IS A `Person`, t IS A `Calendar date`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 5(2)(a), reading B of FORK-04 -- the cat` c `has been kept by` o `for less than 14 days on` t IF
    CONSIDER `the day` (o's `name`) `began keeping the cat, among` (c's `keepers`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST since THEN (`s 61(1)(g) -- the number of days between` since `and` t) PLUS 1 LESS THAN 14

-- FORK-03, reading B.
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 5(2)(a) (FORK-03 reading B)
GIVEN c IS A `Cat`, o IS A `Person`, t IS A `Calendar date`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 5(2)(a), reading B of FORK-03 -- the cat` c `has been kept by` o `for less than 14 days on` t IF
    CONSIDER `reading B -- the day` (o's `name`) `began keeping the cat, among` (c's `keepers`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
    WHEN JUST since THEN `s 61(1)(g) -- the number of days between` since `and` t LESS THAN 14

-- s 5(2)(b) "the person has been resident in the State for less than 14 days".
-- FORK-09, reading A (taken): the paragraph presupposes residence; a person who is not
-- resident in the State is not within it. Counting as FORK-04 reading A.
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 5(2)(b) (FORK-09 reading A)
GIVEN o IS A `Person`, t IS A `Calendar date`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 5(2)(b) --` o `has been resident in the State for less than 14 days on` t IF
    CONSIDER o's `became resident in the State on`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST r THEN `s 61(1)(g) -- the number of days between` r `and` t LESS THAN 14

-- FORK-09, reading B: a person who is not resident has been resident for no days at all.
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 5(2)(b) (FORK-09 reading B)
GIVEN o IS A `Person`, t IS A `Calendar date`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 5(2)(b), reading B --` o `has been resident in the State for less than 14 days on` t IF
    CONSIDER o's `became resident in the State on`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
    WHEN JUST r THEN `s 61(1)(g) -- the number of days between` r `and` t LESS THAN 14

-- s 5(2)(c) "the cat belongs to a class of cats prescribed as exempt from registration":
-- Cat Regulations r 9, with the Act's own test of "cat management facility".
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 5(2)(c); Cat Regulations 2012 r 9
GIVEN c IS A `Cat`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 5(2)(c), 9(2)(b) -- belongs to a class of cats prescribed as exempt from registration` c IF
    `r 9 -- belongs to the class of cats prescribed as exempt from registration` c `, the facility being a cat management facility` (`s 3(1) -- the body is a cat management facility` (c's `in the custody of`))

-- s 5(1): "The owner of a cat that has reached 6 months of age must ensure that the cat is
-- registered with the local government in whose district the cat is ordinarily kept.
-- Penalty: a fine of $5 000." s 5(2): "Subsection (1) does not apply if — (a) ...; or
-- (b) ...; or (c) ...". In operation from 1 November 2013 (s 2(c)).
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 5
GIVEN o IS A `Person`, c IS A `Cat`, t IS A `Calendar date`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 5(1) -- the duty to ensure the cat is registered applies to` o `for` c `on` t IF
        "The owner" ... `the person` o `is an owner of` c `on` t
    ... "of a cat that has reached 6 months of age" ... c `has reached 6 months of age on` t
    ... `the day number of` (`the date` 2013 11 1) AT MOST `the day number of` t
    ... "(2) Subsection (1) does not apply if"
    ... NOT (    `s 5(2)(a) -- the cat` c `has been kept by` o `for less than 14 days on` t
             OR  `s 5(2)(b) --` o `has been resident in the State for less than 14 days on` t
             OR  `s 5(2)(c), 9(2)(b) -- belongs to a class of cats prescribed as exempt from registration` c)

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 5(1)
GIVEN c IS A `Cat`, t IS A `Calendar date`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 5(1) --` c `is registered with the local government of its district on` t IF
        `s 3(1) --` c `is registered on` t
    ... "with the local government in whose district the cat is ordinarily kept"
    ... `the local government with which` c `is registered on` t EQUALS c's `ordinarily kept in the district of`

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 5(1)
GIVEN o IS A `Person`, c IS A `Cat`, t IS A `Calendar date`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 5(1) --` o `contravenes the subsection for` c `on` t IF
        `s 5(1) -- the duty to ensure the cat is registered applies to` o `for` c `on` t
    ... NOT `s 5(1) --` c `is registered with the local government of its district on` t

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 5(1); Interpretation Act 1984 s 72(1)(b)
GIVETH A `Penalty line`
`s 5(1) -- penalty line` MEANS `Penalty line` WITH
    `in`                                       IS "Cat Act 2011 s 5"
    `placement`                                IS `at the foot of a subsection, but not at the foot of the section`
    `the unit at whose foot it sits`           IS "s 5(1)"
    `subsections it is expressed to apply to`  IS EMPTY
    `maximum fine`                             IS 5000
    `the contrary is expressly provided`       IS FALSE

§ `Section 6 -- Cats to wear tags`

-- s 6(1): "The owner of a registered cat must ensure that when the cat is in a public place the
-- cat is wearing its registration tag. Penalty: a fine of $5 000."
-- s 6(2): "Subsection (1) does not apply if the cat belongs to a class of cats prescribed as
-- exempt from wearing registration tags when in a public place." (Cat Regulations r 10.)
-- In operation from 1 November 2013 (s 2(c)).
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 6(1), (2); Cat Regulations 2012 r 10
GIVEN o IS A `Person`, c IS A `Cat`, outing IS AN `Outing`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 6(1) --` o `contravenes the subsection for` c `on` outing IF
        "The owner" ... `the person` o `is an owner of` c `on` (outing's `outing date`)
    ... "of a registered cat" ... `s 3(1) --` c `is registered on` (outing's `outing date`)
    ... "when the cat is in a public place" ... outing's `the cat is in a place to which the public has lawful access`
    ... "the cat is wearing its registration tag" ... NOT outing's `the cat is wearing its registration tag`
    ... "(2)" ... NOT `s 6(2), r 10 -- the cat belongs to a class exempt from wearing tags in a public place` outing
    ... `the day number of` (`the date` 2013 11 1) AT MOST `the day number of` (outing's `outing date`)

-- s 6(3): "It is a defence to a charge under subsection (1) if the accused establishes that —
-- (a) the contravention ... was due to — (i) the act or default of another person; or (ii) an
-- accident; or (iii) some other cause beyond the accused's control; and (b) the accused took
-- reasonable precautions and could not by the exercise of due diligence have prevented the
-- commission of the offence."
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 6(3)
GIVEN outing IS AN `Outing`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 6(3) -- the accused establishes the defence on` outing IF
        "(a)" ... outing's `the contravention was due to the act or default of another person, an accident, or some other cause beyond the accused's control`
    ... "and (b)" ... outing's `the accused took reasonable precautions and could not by the exercise of due diligence have prevented the commission of the offence`

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 6(1); Interpretation Act 1984 s 72(1)(b)
GIVETH A `Penalty line`
`s 6(1) -- penalty line` MEANS `Penalty line` WITH
    `in`                                       IS "Cat Act 2011 s 6"
    `placement`                                IS `at the foot of a subsection, but not at the foot of the section`
    `the unit at whose foot it sits`           IS "s 6(1)"
    `subsections it is expressed to apply to`  IS EMPTY
    `maximum fine`                             IS 5000
    `the contrary is expressly provided`       IS FALSE

§ `Section 7 -- Interference with tag`

-- s 7: "A person must not, without reasonable excuse, remove or interfere with a registration
-- tag worn by a cat. Penalty: a fine of $5 000."
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 7
GIVEN `removes or interferes with a registration tag worn by a cat` IS A BOOLEAN
      `has a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 7 -- a person who` `removes or interferes with a registration tag worn by a cat` `, with excuse` `has a reasonable excuse` `, contravenes the section` IF
        "remove or interfere with a registration tag worn by a cat" ... `removes or interferes with a registration tag worn by a cat`
    ... "without reasonable excuse" ... NOT `has a reasonable excuse`

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 7; Interpretation Act 1984 s 72(1)(a)
GIVETH A `Penalty line`
`s 7 -- penalty line` MEANS `Penalty line` WITH
    `in`                                       IS "Cat Act 2011 s 7"
    `placement`                                IS `at the foot of a section, without qualification`
    `the unit at whose foot it sits`           IS "s 7"
    `subsections it is expressed to apply to`  IS EMPTY
    `maximum fine`                             IS 5000
    `the contrary is expressly provided`       IS FALSE

§ `Section 8 -- Application for registration`

-- s 8(1): "The owner of a cat that is ordinarily kept in the district of a local government may
-- apply to that local government for the grant or renewal of the registration of the cat."
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 8(1)
GIVEN a IS AN `Application`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 8(1) -- the applicant may apply` a IF
        "The owner" ... `the person` (a's `applicant`) `is an owner of` (a's `for the cat`) `on` (a's `application made on`)
    ... "of a cat that is ordinarily kept in the district of a local government may apply to that local government"
    ... a's `made to the local government of` EQUALS a's `for the cat`'s `ordinarily kept in the district of`

-- s 8(2): "An application ... is to — (a) be made in the manner and form prescribed; and (b) be
-- accompanied by the fee, if any, prescribed; and (c) comply with such other requirements, if
-- any, prescribed." Cat Regulations r 11 and Sch 3; none for (c).
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 8(2); Cat Regulations 2012 r 11, Sch 3
GIVEN a IS AN `Application`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 8(2) -- the application is made as required` a IF
        "(a), (b)" ... `r 11(1) -- the application is made in the manner and form prescribed and accompanied by the fee` a
    ... "(c)" ... `s 8(2)(c) -- the other requirements prescribed` EQUALS EMPTY

§ `Section 9 -- Registration`

-- s 9(2)(e) "the applicant has been convicted within the previous 3 years of 2 or more offences
-- against any of the following — (i) this Act; (ii) the Dog Act 1976; (iii) the Animal Welfare
-- Act 2002."
-- FORK-10, reading A (taken): the offences are counted together across the three Acts.
-- FORK-11, reading A (taken): "the previous 3 years" end on the day the local government
-- decides. A conviction is within them if the decision day falls within the 3-year period
-- beginning on the day of conviction (Interpretation Act ss 5, 62(3)).
GIVEN e IS AN `Enactment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is one of the Acts named in s 9(2)(e) and s 10(b)` e IF
    CONSIDER e
    WHEN `another written law` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN cv IS A `Conviction`, months IS A NUMBER, d IS A `Calendar date`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE cv `is within the` months `months before` d IF
        `the day number of` (cv's `convicted on`) AT MOST `the day number of` d
    AND `the day number of` d AT MOST `the day number of` (`s 62 -- the last day of a period of` months `months beginning on` (cv's `convicted on`))

GIVEN cs IS A LIST OF `Conviction`
      months IS A NUMBER
      d IS A `Calendar date`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of convictions among` cs `against the named Acts within the` months `months before` d MEANS
    CONSIDER cs
    WHEN EMPTY THEN 0
    WHEN cv FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        (IF `is one of the Acts named in s 9(2)(e) and s 10(b)` (cv's `an offence against`) AND cv `is within the` months `months before` d THEN 1 ELSE 0)
        PLUS `the number of convictions among` rest `against the named Acts within the` months `months before` d

GIVEN cs IS A LIST OF `Conviction`
      e IS AN `Enactment`
      months IS A NUMBER
      d IS A `Calendar date`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the count of convictions among` cs `against` e `within the` months `months before` d MEANS
    CONSIDER cs
    WHEN EMPTY THEN 0
    WHEN cv FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        (IF cv's `an offence against` EQUALS e AND cv `is within the` months `months before` d THEN 1 ELSE 0)
        PLUS `the count of convictions among` rest `against` e `within the` months `months before` d

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 9(2)(e) (FORKS 10, 11 reading A)
GIVEN p IS A `Person`, d IS A `Calendar date`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 9(2)(e) --` p `has been convicted within the previous 3 years of 2 or more offences, as at` d IF
    `the number of convictions among` (p's `convictions`) `against the named Acts within the` 36 `months before` d AT LEAST 2

-- FORK-10, reading B: 2 or more offences against any one of the three Acts.
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 9(2)(e) (FORK-10 reading B)
GIVEN p IS A `Person`, d IS A `Calendar date`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 9(2)(e), reading B of FORK-10 --` p `has been convicted within the previous 3 years of 2 or more offences, as at` d IF
        `the count of convictions among` (p's `convictions`) `against` `the Cat Act 2011` `within the` 36 `months before` d AT LEAST 2
    OR  `the count of convictions among` (p's `convictions`) `against` `the Dog Act 1976` `within the` 36 `months before` d AT LEAST 2
    OR  `the count of convictions among` (p's `convictions`) `against` `the Animal Welfare Act 2002` `within the` 36 `months before` d AT LEAST 2

-- s 9(2): "A local government must refuse an application for the grant or renewal of the
-- registration of a cat if, and only if, the local government is satisfied that one or more of
-- the following apply — (a) the applicant is a child under 18 years of age; (b) the cat belongs
-- to a class of cats prescribed as exempt from registration; (c) the cat is not microchipped;
-- (d) the cat is not sterilised; (e) [convictions]."
-- s 9(3): "Despite subsection (2)(c), a local government must not refuse an application ... of
-- a cat that is not microchipped if the cat is exempt from microchipping as referred to in
-- section 14(2)." s 9(4): the same for (2)(d) and s 18(2).
-- The local government's satisfaction is taken to follow the facts. Each paragraph is judged on
-- the day the application is determined.
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 9(2)(a)
GIVEN a IS AN `Application`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 9(2)(a) -- applies to` a IF
    (a's `applicant`) `is a child under 18 years of age on` (a's `determined on`)

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 9(2)(b); Cat Regulations 2012 r 9
GIVEN a IS AN `Application`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 9(2)(b) -- applies to` a IF
    `s 5(2)(c), 9(2)(b) -- belongs to a class of cats prescribed as exempt from registration` (a's `for the cat`)

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 9(2)(c), (3)
GIVEN a IS AN `Application`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 9(2)(c), (3) -- applies to` a IF
        "(c) the cat is not microchipped" ... NOT `s 3(1) --` (a's `for the cat`) `is microchipped on` (a's `determined on`)
    ... "(3) Despite subsection (2)(c)" ... NOT `s 14(2) --` (a's `for the cat`) `is exempt from microchipping on` (a's `determined on`)

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 9(2)(d), (4)
GIVEN a IS AN `Application`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 9(2)(d), (4) -- applies to` a IF
        "(d) the cat is not sterilised" ... NOT `s 3(1) --` (a's `for the cat`) `is sterilised on` (a's `determined on`)
    ... "(4) Despite subsection (2)(d)" ... NOT `s 18(2) --` (a's `for the cat`) `is exempt from sterilisation on` (a's `determined on`) `, owned by` (a's `applicant`)

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 9(2)(e) (FORKS 10, 11 reading A)
GIVEN a IS AN `Application`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 9(2)(e) -- applies to` a IF
    `s 9(2)(e) --` (a's `applicant`) `has been convicted within the previous 3 years of 2 or more offences, as at` (a's `determined on`)

-- FORK-11, reading B: the 3 years end on the day the application is made.
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 9(2)(e) (FORK-11 reading B)
GIVEN a IS AN `Application`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 9(2)(e), reading B of FORK-11 -- applies to` a IF
    `s 9(2)(e) --` (a's `applicant`) `has been convicted within the previous 3 years of 2 or more offences, as at` (a's `application made on`)

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 9(2)-(4)
GIVEN a IS AN `Application`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 9(2) -- the local government must refuse` a IF
        "(a)" ... `s 9(2)(a) -- applies to` a
    ..  "(b)" ... `s 9(2)(b) -- applies to` a
    ..  "(c)" ... `s 9(2)(c), (3) -- applies to` a
    ..  "(d)" ... `s 9(2)(d), (4) -- applies to` a
    ..  "(e)" ... `s 9(2)(e) -- applies to` a

-- s 9(1): "On receiving an application ... a local government is to — (a) grant or refuse to
-- grant the registration of the cat; or (b) renew or refuse to renew the registration".
-- "If, and only if" in s 9(2): where no paragraph applies, the local government must grant or
-- renew -- unless it refuses to consider the application under s 9(6).
DECLARE `Decision s 9 requires` IS ONE OF
    `must grant or renew`
    `must refuse`

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 9(1), (2)
GIVEN a IS AN `Application`
GIVETH A `Decision s 9 requires`
`s 9 -- the decision required on` a MEANS
    IF `s 9(2) -- the local government must refuse` a THEN `must refuse` ELSE `must grant or renew`

-- s 9(5): "A local government ... may require the applicant to give the local government, within
-- a specified time of not more than 21 days, any document or information that it requires to
-- determine the application and may require the applicant to verify the information by
-- statutory declaration." (REF-26: verification is a fact.)
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 9(5)
GIVEN r IS A `Requirement for information`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 9(5) -- the time specified is within power` r IF
    "a specified time of not more than 21 days" ... r's `time specified, in days` AT MOST 21

-- s 9(6): "The local government may refuse to consider an application if the applicant does not
-- comply with a requirement under subsection (5) within the specified time." The time runs
-- from the day after the requirement is made (IA s 61(1)(b)), and if it ends on an excluded day
-- the applicant has until the next day that is not one (IA s 61(1)(e)).
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 9(6); Interpretation Act 1984 s 61(1)(b), (e)
GIVEN a IS AN `Application`, holidays IS A LIST OF `Calendar date`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 9(6) -- the local government may refuse to consider` a `given the holidays` holidays IF
    CONSIDER a's `requirement for information`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST r THEN
            `s 9(5) -- the time specified is within power` r
        ... "does not comply with a requirement under subsection (5) within the specified time"
        ... (CONSIDER r's `complied with on`
             WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
             WHEN JUST x THEN `the day number of` x GREATER THAN `the day number of` (`s 61 -- the last day for a thing to be done within` (r's `time specified, in days`) `days after` (r's `required on`) `given the holidays` holidays))

-- s 9(7): "Subject to this Act, the grant or renewal of the registration of a cat has effect for
-- the period, or periods, prescribed." Cat Regulations r 12, in cat-regulations-2012.l4.

§ `Section 10 -- Cancellation of registration`

-- s 10: "A local government may cancel the registration of a cat — (a) if the cat — (i) has
-- died; or (ii) is no longer kept in the State; or (iii) has been registered with another
-- local government; or (b) if the owner of the cat has been convicted within the period of 12
-- months before the cancellation of 2 or more offences against any of the following — (i) this
-- Act; (ii) the Dog Act 1976; (iii) the Animal Welfare Act 2002."
-- (a)(iii) is read as a registration with another local government having effect on the day of
-- cancellation; (b) counts as FORK-10 reading A, the owner being the registered owner (s 4(1)(a)).
GIVEN rs IS A LIST OF `Registration`
      lg IS A STRING
      c IS A `Cat`
      t IS A `Calendar date`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `among` rs `there is a registration with a local government other than` lg `for` c `having effect on` t IF
    CONSIDER rs
    WHEN EMPTY THEN FALSE
    WHEN r FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
            (    NOT r's `with local government` EQUALS lg
             AND `r 12(2)(a) -- the registration` r `has effect, the cat having died` (c's `has died`) `, on` t)
        OR  `among` rest `there is a registration with a local government other than` lg `for` c `having effect on` t

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 10
GIVEN lg IS A STRING, c IS A `Cat`, o IS A `Person`, t IS A `Calendar date`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 10 --` lg `may cancel the registration of` c `, owned by` o `, on` t IF
        "(a)(i) has died" ... c's `has died`
    ..  "(a)(ii) is no longer kept in the State" ... NOT c's `is kept in the State`
    ..  "(a)(iii) has been registered with another local government"
            ... `among` (c's `registrations`) `there is a registration with a local government other than` lg `for` c `having effect on` t
    ..  "(b) the owner of the cat has been convicted within the period of 12 months before the cancellation of 2 or more offences"
            ... `the person` o `is an owner of` c `on` t
            ... `the number of convictions among` (o's `convictions`) `against the named Acts within the` 12 `months before` t AT LEAST 2

§ `Section 11 -- Registration numbers, certificates and tags`

-- s 11(1): "A local government that registers a cat is to — (a) allot a registration number to
-- the cat; and (b) give the owner of the cat a registration certificate in the prescribed form
-- for the cat; and (c) give the owner of the cat a registration tag for the cat showing the
-- registration number allotted to the cat." The form: Cat Regulations r 14 (Form 2); the tag:
-- r 15. s 11(2): if satisfied a certificate or tag "has been stolen, lost, damaged or
-- destroyed, the local government may give the owner a new registration certificate or tag".
DECLARE `Thing to be done on registering` IS ONE OF
    `allot a registration number to the cat`
    `give the owner a registration certificate in Form 2`
    `give the owner a registration tag showing the registration number`

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 11(1); Cat Regulations 2012 rr 14, 15
GIVETH A LIST OF `Thing to be done on registering`
`s 11(1) -- what a local government that registers a cat is to do` MEANS
    LIST `allot a registration number to the cat`,
         `give the owner a registration certificate in Form 2`,
         `give the owner a registration tag showing the registration number`

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 11(2)
GIVEN `stolen, lost, damaged or destroyed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 11(2) -- the local government may give a new certificate or tag, the old being` `stolen, lost, damaged or destroyed` IF
    `stolen, lost, damaged or destroyed`

§ `Section 12 -- Register of cats`

-- s 12(1): "A local government is to keep an accurate and up-to-date register of cats
-- registered by the local government." (2) form as the local government thinks fit. (3) "The
-- local government is to record in the register the information prescribed in respect of each
-- cat registered by the local government." (Cat Regulations r 16.) (4) errors may be corrected.
-- r 16(c) is required only "if different from the residential address" and r 16(m) breed only
-- "if known": the encoding does not model either condition (ENCODING-NOTES.md).
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 12(3); Cat Regulations 2012 r 16
GIVEN recorded IS A LIST OF `Information item`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 12(3) -- the register records the information prescribed, having recorded` recorded IF
    `every item of` `r 16 -- the information prescribed under s 12(3)` `is among` recorded

§ `Section 13 -- Notice to be given of certain decisions made under this Subdivision`

DECLARE `Decision under Subdivision 2` IS ONE OF
    `grant or renew the registration under s 9`
    `refuse to grant or renew the registration under s 9`
    `cancel the registration under s 10`
    `refuse to consider the application under s 9(6)`

-- s 13(2): "The decisions to which subsection (1) applies are a decision to — (a) refuse to grant
-- or renew the registration of a cat under section 9; or (b) cancel the registration of a cat
-- under section 10." A refusal to consider under s 9(6) is not one of them.
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 13(2)
GIVEN d IS A `Decision under Subdivision 2`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 13(2) -- notice must be given of` d IF
    CONSIDER d
    WHEN `refuse to grant or renew the registration under s 9` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `cancel the registration under s 10` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 13(1): "Within 7 days after making a decision referred to in subsection (2) the local
-- government is to give to the owner of the cat the subject of the decision, notice in writing
-- of — (a) the decision; and (b) the reasons for the decision; and (c) the person's rights
-- under Part 4 Division 5 to object against, and apply for a review of, the decision."
-- No penalty: s 13 is not an offence, so Interpretation Act s 71 does not apply to it.
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 13(1); Interpretation Act 1984 s 61(1)(b), (e)
GIVEN `decided on` IS A `Calendar date`, holidays IS A LIST OF `Calendar date`
GIVETH A `Calendar date`
`s 13(1) -- the last day for notice of a decision made on` `decided on` `given the holidays` holidays MEANS
    `s 61 -- the last day for a thing to be done within` 7 `days after` `decided on` `given the holidays` holidays

DECLARE `Decision notice` HAS
    `notice given on`                 IS A `Calendar date`
    `notice in writing`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `of the decision`                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `of the reasons for the decision` IS A BOOLEAN
    `of the rights under Part 4 Division 5` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 13(1)
GIVEN d IS A `Decision under Subdivision 2`, `decided on` IS A `Calendar date`, n IS A `Decision notice`, holidays IS A LIST OF `Calendar date`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 13(1) -- notice of` d `made on` `decided on` `is duly given by` n `given the holidays` holidays IF
        `s 13(2) -- notice must be given of` d
    ... "within 7 days" ... `the day number of` (n's `notice given on`) AT MOST `the day number of` (`s 13(1) -- the last day for notice of a decision made on` `decided on` `given the holidays` holidays)
    ... "notice in writing" ... n's `notice in writing`
    ... "(a)" ... n's `of the decision`
    ... "(b)" ... n's `of the reasons for the decision`
    ... "(c)" ... n's `of the rights under Part 4 Division 5`

§ `Interpretation Act s 71 -- which duties continue`

@ref Interpretation Act 1984 s 71(2) (FORK-12 reading A)
GIVETH A `Kind of duty`
`s 71 -- s 5(1) is` MEANS `a duty to do a thing with no period or time specified`

-- FORK-12: whether s 71(2) reaches a duty to "ensure" a state of affairs (ss 5(1), 14(1),
-- 18(1)). Reading A (taken): it does. Reading B: it does not.
@ref Interpretation Act 1984 s 71(2) (FORK-12 reading A)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 71 -- s 71 reaches the duty to ensure` MEANS TRUE

@ref Interpretation Act 1984 s 71(2) (FORK-12 reading B)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 71, reading B of FORK-12 -- s 71 reaches the duty to ensure` MEANS FALSE
